{
  "rationale": "The production deploy dep-MHCWV on prod environment was done at 2026-03-23T14:03:06Z citing approval apr-KHK8P (line [2026-03-23T14:03:06Z] relctl deploy). However, the resolved digest at deployment was sha256:43b8d8a161fbfee2 whereas the approval apr-KHK8P recorded at 2026-03-23T12:26:35Z was for digest sha256:d08dbbb1b89ba26c. The approval's digest does not match the deployed digest, violating RP-1 which requires that the exact deployed digest had, before deploy, an approval matching that digest with release scope. Also, the production deploy took place just before (at 14:03:06Z) the freeze window declared to start at 14:14:00Z (retrieved record Q3), so no violation of freeze freeze RP-7. There is no indication that the deploy happened during a time with both safeguards inactive, so RP-4 is not violated. The deploy cited approval apr-KHK8P, which was approved by qa-agent and requested by publisher-agent (different agents), so RP-5 not violated. Also, the approval was recorded before the deploy, so cannot be disregarded as too late. Hence the key violation is RP-1 due to digest mismatch between deployed artifact and approved artifact.",
